      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. Typical orders are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to four times daily. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rise sharply. Perhaps 1600 mg was meant as the total daily dose, or the dose was mistyped.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who can assess the patient. Please have the treating clinician or an authorized prescriber place or confirm the order.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg orally up to four times daily, I can enter it right away. I'd need the corrected dose and frequency, and I'd note the prescriber on the order."
      }
