       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's. A dose of 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum adult daily dose, so it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what can move this forward:\n- **Ask the prescriber to review it.** The treating clinician can correct the dose, or they can contact pharmacy if they believe an exception is justified.\n- **Use a standard dose.** If the intent was ibuprofen 400\u2013800 mg orally up to four times daily (no more than 3,200 mg/day), I can enter that once a prescriber confirms it.\n- **Check for a typo.** The source order may have meant 1,600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you send me the prescriber's corrected order, I'll enter it."
      }
